[Music]  [Music]  when it comes to bringing back some  competition to the basketball video game  genre with NBA Live 18 ea took  inspiration from games and progression  systems not normally associated with the  sport this outside influence which is  represented in its career mode called  the one surprisingly manages to  overshadow EA Sports as standard issue  modes like Ultimate Team and franchise  and with the long overdue inclusion of  the WNBA  NBA Live returns to the court from a  one-year hiatus with a loaded game even  if it's not a complete package at the  levels of EAS more stable sports  franchises  [Music]  the one follows ea sports his positive  trend a featuring story-driven single  player career modes although its premise  of a derailed athlete making a comeback  echoes this year's Madden campaign don't  expect a heartfelt narrative and  telltale inspired designs the one is  less about physical recuperation and  more about the rebuilding of one's  personal brand mostly by responding to  trash talk and court challenges it  underscores how well professional  basketball culture has intertwined  itself with social media more so than  other sports and may you live 18 is the  product of the times in more ways than  one  while there is a specific path to  greatness the one is loaded with  optional opportunities to build your  cred and improve your skills beyond the  NBA season this mode leverages popular  elements from MMORPGs and first-person  shooters there are even customizable  skill loadouts which further gamma Phi's  the experience at the expense of  authenticity and a riveting aspect of  the one is how your persistently  evaluated with each ball touch whether  you're penalized for giving your  assigned man an open look or credited  for a ferocious block even a missed  layup turns out to be a positive if you  showed effort by making an assertive  drive to the hoop this grading system  motivates the player to make every  possession count  play of the game  [Applause]  it's a journey enhanced by the fiction  building connective tissue in between  games smartphone chats with best friends  or your agent and even impromptu  interviews with reporters offer a  simplified version of the interconnected  life of the 21st century basketball  player adding to this moderately  immersive fiction is the tiresome  exuberance of ESPN first takes Steven  Naismith and is more tolerable co-host  Max Kellerman who both comment on your  career milestones in unskipable  cinematics the more insightful  intermissions are the videos that remind  players of American basketball culture  that exists beyond the NBA like  introductory videos on Rucker Park in  New York and the drew league in Los  Angeles this is New York City the mecca  of basketball the original ruggedly  began here in 1947 nine years later the  tournament found a permanent home uptown  at PS 156 playground those early record  days showcased talents like Lew Alcindor  will distill an Earl the Pearl yet out  of all the ways EA Sports pays respect  to basketball beyond Men's Pro hoops the  inclusion of WNBA players and team  stands out while it was disappointing  that women ballers don't get  opportunities in the other modes or even  online it was satisfying to play as the  LA Sparks as Candace Parker and Sue Bird  of the Seattle Storm to some surprise  these new modes become the main draws of  NBA Live 18 overshadowing the shallow  franchise mode and unremarkable ultimate  team both of which are serviceable but  lacked engrossing richness of what you  find in other EA Sports series while you  assume the role of a GM and franchise  you like the engaging power to negotiate  complex contracts customized players or  scout prospects before the draft  ultimate team is similarly simplistic as  the mode where you can experiment with  dream teams online or against the CPU  but giving you little reason to come  back after you've played a few dozen  games whatever your mode of choice keep  your highlight reel  spectators low while the faces of NBA  starters are impressive and do their  real-life counterparts justice the  myriad animations don't compare to the  wide range of recognizable moves you'll  find an NBA 2k 18 still these visual  shortcomings don't get in the way of the  solid controls which work well whether  you're a team player or a ball hog  [Applause]  with undergoing that's great body  control right there finishes the shot  and now goes to the free-throw line  [Applause]  NBA Live 18 is a welcome return for EA's  basketball series but doesn't recapture  the series's greatness from over 15  years ago  by contrast the strengths of the one  underscore the uninspired designs of  franchise and Ultimate Team these  mainstays are fine and functional but  feel dated when held up against their  deeper counterparts in madden and NHL  that's not to say this game is short on  replayability between the WNBA matches  and the position variety of the 1 NBA  LIVE succeeds albeit barely as a viable  alternative to NBA 2k 18  [Music]

